<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ja'far Pishevari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1947">1947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Seyyed Ja'far Pishevari</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ja'far Pishevari was an Iranian Azerbaijani communist who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> People's Government, set up in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> in 1945 under Soviet occupation. A veteran of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilan">Gilan</a> Soviet Republic and long imprisoned under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reza-shah">Reza Shah</a>, he founded the Azerbaijan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-party-uganda">Democratic Party</a> in September 1945. When Soviet troops withdrew in 1946 the Iranian army reoccupied Tabriz, and he fled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, where he died in a car accident in 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jafar-pishevari.jpg" alt="Ja'far Pishevari" width="320" height="499" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pishavari.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
